<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:20Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>US judge temporarily blocks Trump's arch project after panel approval</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45ad0899d179bd998fdeaa0028e8d5cdcdf6b529d2f4762c4b4486d4ccb44261</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:02:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T06:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-judge-temporarily-blocks-trump-s-arch-project-after-panel-approval/a-79871690--3c90724774bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-judge-temporarily-blocks-trump-s-arch-project-after-panel-approval/a-79871690?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A judge ordered a two-week stop to construction on US President Trump's arch project in Washington. A federal panel had approved Trump's triumphal arch plans in an 8-4 vote.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ex-lawmaker jailed in Macau's first national security trial</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd44c480510fe5c189c710d0949ca2a487f1201daca0659d89590a9e561e249e</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:02:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T04:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ex-lawmaker-jailed-in-macau-s-first-national-security-trial/a-79871673--02ef64bcc21e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ex-lawmaker-jailed-in-macau-s-first-national-security-trial/a-79871673?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pro-democracy former lawmaker Au Kam San was found guilty of "subversion against the political power of the State." He was handed a prison sentence of 12-and-a-half years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Asian stocks slump after US tech rout amid AI jitters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:708ac65d0fdba7828cbd1233a2c1c6289fa7f3a207e46c1765525a3d854f5fb6</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:02:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T02:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/asian-stocks-slump-after-us-tech-rout-amid-ai-jitters/a-79871504--b7d3eaa80f9c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/asian-stocks-slump-after-us-tech-rout-amid-ai-jitters/a-79871504?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Concerns that Democrats in the US will push back against data center projects are weighing on an AI trade that is already on shaky footing amid growing doubts about profitability.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump raises prospect of 'big, beautiful' Russia-Ukraine deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:085939253cf96e717503f8827af9b4cff3b517775788483cfd9ce1ab622c6cf9</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:02:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T23:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-raises-prospect-of-big-beautiful-russia-ukraine-deal/a-79871394--3dda57bca4be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-raises-prospect-of-big-beautiful-russia-ukraine-deal/a-79871394?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said the Ukraine war was close to being settled and that ending it might involve "all of Europe." Trump has previously made several similar promises, with no resolution to the conflict in sight.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Austrian tycoon Rene Benko sentenced to 2 years in prison for fraud</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2409df1b9a5a34b4b7df95be8be28b3040aa117c77bf9f3cc429e8c8d30ea8e</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:02:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T20:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/austrian-tycoon-rene-benko-sentenced-to-2-years-in-prison-for-fraud/a-79870056--6947b2681495.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/austrian-tycoon-rene-benko-sentenced-to-2-years-in-prison-for-fraud/a-79870056?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Austrian businessman Rene Benko, who suffered a major fall from grace after his real estate empire, Signa Holding, went bust, was handed two more years in prison.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Gavin Newsom commutes sentences of all death row inmates in California</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6084c8696db5344f23a1f1f5249a20b6ff0c0b3d4a46ed595dfcc438cf006d61</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:02:59Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T20:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gavin-newsom-commutes-sentences-of-all-death-row-inmates-in-california/a-79870988--44297dcec5b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gavin-newsom-commutes-sentences-of-all-death-row-inmates-in-california/a-79870988?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Gavin Newsom, a Democrat and a rumored presidential candidate, moved to commute the death sentences of 548 inmates in California for one of his last acts as governor of the state.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Americans voted against Trump's Iran war. Gulf countries hope that means an end to the conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2ec389c98e54fbc7f0a2a920d19d091ec0b79895fb110c20c3d4f62271a5e69</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T19:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/americans-voted-against-trump-s-iran-war-gulf-countries-hope-that-means-an-end-to-the-conflict/a-79868398--8084b702dfa9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/americans-voted-against-trump-s-iran-war-gulf-countries-hope-that-means-an-end-to-the-conflict/a-79868398?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US midterm results showed how unpopular Donald Trump's Iran war is. Now, Gulf countries, trapped for months in the middle of the war between the US and Iran, see reason for optimism.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Pete Hegseth under fire as Republicans trade blame for midterm debacle</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d9da60a0daa314a84ae04995da3b52a1ef9d4a884dd35c2a93d90733de96aec</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T19:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pete-hegseth-under-fire-as-republicans-trade-blame-for-midterm-debacle/a-79869867--678f4ce412f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pete-hegseth-under-fire-as-republicans-trade-blame-for-midterm-debacle/a-79869867?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran war hawk Pete Hegseth is facing the fallout from Republicans' midterms losses as high energy prices turned voters toward Democrats. US President Trump continues to support his embattled defense chief — for now.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Does the Oleshky ceasefire signal progress to come in Ukraine?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:497c0e15b2af415eca617c9fec884d7621a0ebef1a010c8afed3d57d612e4944</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T18:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/does-the-oleshky-ceasefire-signal-progress-to-come-in-ukraine/a-79869164--aae9565ed50c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/does-the-oleshky-ceasefire-signal-progress-to-come-in-ukraine/a-79869164?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of civilians were evacuated from the city of Oleshky after Russia and Ukraine agreed to a US-brokered ceasefire. Some observers have expressed optimism that more such humanitarian missions might follow.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>France: More than 600,000 protest as anger grows over cost of living</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:849ea2991d646abede60eaf02a784d726cc1ab2360ffe64a3d237899109c26b5</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T17:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-more-than-600-000-protest-as-anger-grows-over-cost-of-living/a-79860616--706971383a01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-more-than-600-000-protest-as-anger-grows-over-cost-of-living/a-79860616?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Demonstrators took to the streets in several French cities to call for government action on the high cost of living. Protests were largely peaceful, but there were some reports of escalation, including in Paris.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Arrests and investigations as Serbia begins post-election clean-up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e45ead077ec235e31bbe327b6e4cacc703734e977a6c6da554f6b7cfe5fabcdb</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T17:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/arrests-and-investigations-as-serbia-begins-post-election-clean-up/a-79868652--133f253d322e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/arrests-and-investigations-as-serbia-begins-post-election-clean-up/a-79868652?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The landslide victory of the Students' List in Serbia's general election seems to have removed a blockage in the justice system: Cases that were long stalled are now suddenly moving forward.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany’s Gen Z protests spark debate on integration, bias</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:482cc21e1b6cab81baecbdf8b270656bc63fcfcb3b3fca51f648258b1c9fc6e3</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T16:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-gen-z-protests-spark-debate-on-integration-bias/a-79868497--c2e5ae27f840.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-gen-z-protests-spark-debate-on-integration-bias/a-79868497?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Political debate about the recent Gen Z riots have raised the question: Can Germany talk about problems with integration without putting entire groups of people under suspicion?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Paraguay: President Pena resigns amid bank crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:654be4556c7061eaf25c71d1dafcabcd6e4bfac2cf2570b8be17f36e7b0df52d</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T16:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/paraguay-president-pena-resigns-amid-bank-crisis/a-79868484--620df463270d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/paraguay-president-pena-resigns-amid-bank-crisis/a-79868484?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Paraguay's President Santiago Pena has resigned amid a crisis over his ties to collapsed lender Ueno. Millions of customers' accounts are frozen, with public pension and health care funds also tied up.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>British comedian and actor Russell Brand found guilty of rape</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a01e0131cc671cb1488f2857dce48a4a479b86d13488edf035e2fa9a1538ba7f</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/british-comedian-and-actor-russell-brand-found-guilty-of-rape/a-79867216--4d18f4874d57.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/british-comedian-and-actor-russell-brand-found-guilty-of-rape/a-79867216?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prosecutors labeled Brand a sexual predator. He was charged in sexual assault cases spanning from 1999 to 2009.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran signals satisfaction, skepticism after US midterm vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ca23c0d3b2589169b5b7d1ef87e04987ed1daf0da3c019853636b2e65d1a7f2</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-signals-satisfaction-skepticism-after-us-midterm-vote/a-79867149--f14e22022dc8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-signals-satisfaction-skepticism-after-us-midterm-vote/a-79867149?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While the Iranian regime says the US midterms will not change Washington's policy toward Tehran, some officials and commentators see the resounding Democratic victory as blowback against the Iran war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Who is drug testing Russia's athletes, now that they have returned to international competition?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f45288be514bf3f49d91818f105854900acfdfa29dd3db7e35c64812f915962c</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-is-drug-testing-russia-s-athletes-now-that-they-have-returned-to-international-competition/a-79862467--23bc7b6e6570.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-is-drug-testing-russia-s-athletes-now-that-they-have-returned-to-international-competition/a-79862467?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DW has found that three-quarters of Russia's weightlifting team had no independent out-of-competition testing before this year's world championships, despite the country's doping history.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><titl